   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/954d77971a528b1c.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Megansimmer/The Science Creative Quarterly)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The image shows two proteins involed in the bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE, the mad cow disease). The protein on the left is healthy. The protein on the right is accumulating extra plated sheets, which cause it to become nonfunctional.</p>\n<p>What agent would be causing this fold on the protein?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1247058,
     "content_html": "Bacteria."
    },
    {
     "id": 1247057,
     "content_html": "Viruses."
    },
    {
     "id": 1247056,
     "content_html": "Viroids."
    },
    {
     "id": 1247059,
     "content_html": "Prions."
    }
